{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/39072-creative-sidereal-doom-challenge","id":39072,"title":"Creative Sidereal Doom Challenge!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-29T20:22:56-08:00","id":39072,"title":"Creative Sidereal Doom Challenge!","content":"Ok the books talk a lot about how Sidereals do all sorts of weird things like making sure someone is fed fish instead of pork or other random stuff to make sure fate goes right. Well building on that I would love to see some examples of what happens when they don't. Say they are being harassed by audits in Yu-Shan like never before and just can't send the people to do the jobs they should and something big and bad happens to remind everyone that the Sidereals do an important job and this sort of stuff needs looking after. This doesn't have to be world ending just something suitable to justify the work they do maintaining the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T21:32:01-08:00","id":39111,"title":"","content":"Dark Onyx, Magistrate of the Hundred Kingdoms, was having an excellent day. The magistrate had woken to clear blue skies and gentle breezes, and every little thing since then had gone well. Two of his cases that day had been re-scheduled, and his most odious and annoying scribe was absent with a touch of influenza. An hour ago, he had adjourned to his favorite teahouse, and had a stimulating conversation with the second daughter of a local nobleman; she had been quite responsive to his gentle probes about her marriage prospects, and had agreed to meet with him later to discuss certain possibilities. If that went well, Onyx thought, this day could yet evolve into the best day he'd <i>ever had</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Comes now the accused, Marlan Ske!&quot; boomed his bailiff, interrupting the magistrate's thoughts. &quot;You stand accused of the sale of Dreamwine. How do you plead?&quot;<br /> <br /> Dark Onyx sighed, the details of this particular infraction bubbling up into his memory. Ske was the scion of a merchant house, caught attempting to purloin the restricted substance in order to improve his house's failing fortunes. As far as drugs went, Dreamwine was relatively harmless- it was nothing but a potent beverage which had the pleasant side-effect of creating vivid and happy dreams in subjects. The ban was a political matter, for the local Guild factors had insisted that they be the sole suppliers of the expensive draught, and the nobility had bowed to them like reeds in the wind.<br /> <br /> &quot;Guilty, sirs.&quot; the youth said, face bright with determination, &quot;But I have come to regret my actions, and I throw myself upon the mercies of this court.&quot;<br /> <br /> The general punishment for an infraction like this was either a fine or three years of labor, Onyx knew. It occurred to him, looking on Ske's face, that the boy's familial troubles were also due to the Guild factors, and he felt a twinge of sympathy for the boy. While Magistrate Onyx was not known for his mercies, it seemed to him that the family Ske had already been sorely used by the Guild, and that a verdict here could break them entirely. Filled with this unusual empathy, and suffused by the positive attitude of the day, the Magistrate decided there and then to make a most unusual decision.<br /> <br /> &quot;Very well. It is the judgment of this court that Marlan Ske has repented his minor infraction, and so his sentence shall be a public apology followed by three days of fasting in the temple of the Shogun of Humility.&quot;<br /> <br /> As Magistrate Dark Onyx watched the disbelief and joy rise in Ske's face, he smiled himself, feeling that the world was a very good place indeed.<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> In another world, Nine Secret Steps, Chosen of Journeys, is not caught up in the Gethamane Incident, and is not trapped for two weeks when crystals of frozen time envelop that region. As a result, Steps is able to reach the Hundred Kingdoms and introduce a mild alchemical agent to Dark Onyx's tea on a bright spring day. After Onyx empties the contents of his stomach upon his lovely (and horrified) dining companion, he spends the rest of his day in a dark mood, and so rejects a plea for mercy from the scion of the house of Ske, sentencing him to labor and the full fine, and breaking that house's finances.<br /> <br /> In another world, Marlan Ske meets an eccentric jeweler and artificer in a penal colony, and four years later, the two begin a successful business enterprise selling a series of clever signalling-mirrors to the procurement agents of the Realm. These devices, which can signal company-to-company for miles and require no thaumaturgy, allows the Realm unprecedented battlefield communications, and the Houses re-allocate their essence-wielders to other positions.<br /> <br /> Two years later, in the Battle of Twelve Dragons, the armies of the Realm join with emergency companies from across the Threshold to do battle with the twelve Unshaped Raksha unleashed by agents of the Mask of Winters. Thanks to their sorcerous efficiency and communications, the Realm is able to divert an ambush set by a small army of fae-blooded cultists of the Unshaped, thereby averting potential calamity and preventing the Unshaped from plunging several hundred miles of inland Threshold into the Deep Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T23:39:02-08:00","id":45419,"title":"","content":"I realized I should post one of my own when I was doing this. So!<br /> <br /> Snowfall is a rather plain and normal enough small village in the distant north. Also the east. 12 years before the Empress disappeared someone was born who shouldn't have. A soul intended for a child in the east ended up in a child in the north who should not have drawn breath. This mixed up certain threads in the Loom of Fate though the Loom Spiders are talented and mostly dealt with the issue. They kept the issue from growing to anything larger however there were complications they were quick to send a message to the Sidereals to deal with. Now leaving through the village's easternmost gate will put you on a road in the east. If you are in the east you can find the perpetually snowbound village but somehow if you want your way in you must pass through the easternmost gate. Leaving from anywhere but the easternmost gate leaves you in the north.<br /> <br /> However Sidereals are busy people and the Convention of Wood had other priorities at the time other than an apparently contained glitch in the Loom. Then the Empress vanished, the Solar returned and this matter kept getting pushed back and back. Yet perhaps they should have played closer attention to the matter. The Loom Spiders are not perfect. They did what they could but sometimes those who leave through the east gate will after a time find themselves surprisingly in a snowy plain. Barren but for the bare snow clad trees these poor souls become lost and eventually pass away in the strange cold land. These people who died would again complicate things but for the hard work of the Loom Spiders, who would again send their chittering demands for Sidereals to fix it, changing the minor destinies of people around those who are lost to handle the problem. However the Guild has learned of the place and sees a way to cut so much time off trips between the two regions and are preparing to exploit the quirk while knowing nothing of the larger picture. Now it is only a matter of time before a person with a major destiny ends up getting lost.<br /> <br /> The loss of a big fate could lead to far wider issues. At best perhaps a few demons slip free to make trouble in Creation. At worst the place could fall into the wyld become a beachhead for a major Fair Folk invasion of the north...or maybe the east.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T14:34:34-08:00","id":49296,"title":"","content":"It is often said that many small leaks sink a great ship, and this is applicable to more than ships, of course. First, it was the meeting between a mortal and one of the many gods of Grand Fork, then two of them having a night of carousing where they ended up suggesting the offspring of that union marry the other's god-blooded daughter as celebration of their good fortune. These two children worked well with one another, living happily, even with a near miss with the husband almost dying. Their gratitude brought forth a child they celebrated, whom they called Auspicious Dancer. They were happy. Their child was healthy and beautiful, ever loving all tales and favoring the stories, like one of the great patrons. High hopes were placed upon them, and in order to give more knowledge about the world, the family took a journey to Grey Falls in order to expose the child to Realm ways. It was hoped perhaps a Dynast match could be made, but it was never to be: The child's very charm and great beauty made them a target. Caught up and sold into slavery, the stricken parents searched for many years, to no avail.<br /> <br /> Auspicious Dancer was gone, while Sweetsong Wren was born.<br /> <br /> There was no Sidereal interfering with the god that bore their mother, nor the good night that caused the coupling, nor one to distract the slaver who caught sight of the child without veils to begin with and in the end, a dancer taught a young slave being trained in the courtesan arts how to not just dance, but perhaps to be able to defend themselves in a hidden art, handed master-to-student from days unknown, unknown masters both advancing and corrupting the art and making it look like mere beautiful dance. It was laughable against any kind of essence-driven fighter but useful to keep away unwanted mortals and to draw forth the fortitude both mentally and physically to deal with the state of being a slave without truly losing oneself completely.<br /> <br /> It was also the means that gave Sweetsong Wren the means to begin to be able to fulfill their destiny.<br /> <br /> There was no sidereal to encourage a lesser scion from buying a new slave, appealing to his piety and bringing forth a mighty and fair-minded monk. There was no great hero in Grand Fork to bring it to a new era by the name of Auspicious Dancer nor a daughter to unite houses called Joyous Sun. Instead, the lesser scion died under the ministrations of one of the most beautiful Chosen of Saturn to ever live, ruling his house as his 'heir' and putting it in order, while allowing part of it to weaken in important ways. While it did not fall, it allowed certain Exalts to pass unmolested to a safer country.<br /> Two years, a sidereal finally does come, but this time it is much too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T23:23:47-08:00","id":50473,"title":"","content":"Ooh, interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}